# Keep the build context small and — more importantly — keep secrets and
# local state out of the image.
#
# Docker matches a pattern WITHOUT a leading `**/` against root-relative paths
# only (unlike .gitignore, where `.env*` matches at any depth), so everything
# that must be excluded wherever it sits is listed twice: bare (root) and with
# `**/`. `COPY . .` (builder) and `COPY --from=builder /app/prisma|public`
# (runner) would otherwise carry a developer's prisma/.env, a stray key or a
# nested node_modules into the image layers.
# tests/security/deploy-config.test.ts feeds this file to a Docker-semantics
# matcher and pins the cases below.

# dependencies / build output (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
dist
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# VCS, CI and editor/tool state
.git
**/.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# every env file (.env, .env.local, .env.production, ...) at ANY depth.
# Configuration is injected at runtime via compose `env_file`; nothing secret
# may be baked in. The template is the only env-looking file that is kept, and
# `!.env.example` must stay AFTER the `**/.env*` line (the last match wins).
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example

# credentials and registry config, wherever they sit. If a private registry
# token is ever needed at build time use a BuildKit secret mount
# (`RUN --mount=type=secret`), never a copied .npmrc.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.npmrc

# not needed to build or run the app
tests
test-results
playwright-report
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
npm-debug.log*
